  "notes": "Modified/cash basis village. Governmental = General, Street, CRA funds (Total column p4). Proprietary = Water, Sewer, Solid Waste (Garbage) (Total column p6). Governmental interest income 20,833 is printed below Total Receipts (other financing section) so recorded as receipt with outside_printed_total; transfers in 272,131 and out 194,163 from same section. Governmental disbursements p4 are listed by object; mixed lines are split by fund column (General -> general government, Street -> streets/highways, CRA -> economic development), and the column amounts tie to the printed 627,437 (the Total column's Supplies 30,923 is 1 more than its columns 30,922). The Statement of Activities p2 instead shows General Government 215,090, Public Works 181,810, Culture and Recreation 202,537 (599,437, excluding the 28,000 Elwood Care Center payment); the General Fund departments schedule (p10) splits the General column by department, so General-column object lines are split by department: General -> general government, Library and Community Improvement -> culture/recreation (100,777 here plus Community Improvement capital outlay 10,404 kept as capital outlay = p9 Culture and recreation 111,181), Cemetery -> health/welfare (3,816, matches p9). p10 Supplies and Other rows are off by 1 against their Total column; the General department piece takes the remainder. Business-type roll-forward uses net position (301,806 -> 314,359); cash-flow statement p7-8 shows cash 302,254 -> 314,697 (difference is taxes payable). Business-type transfers net -77,968 matches governmental net transfers, plus net of unfavorable rounding. Balance sheet = Statement of Net Position cash basis Total column (governmental + proprietary), p1; component unit (Elwood Care Center) excluded. Detail: General Fund combining schedule p10 used for General Fund (supersedes the all-funds budget schedule lines for General Fund functions); budget schedule p9 (all funds, combined revenues) used only for Street, CRA and utility funds' expenditures with final budget (budget schedule has no per-fund utility revenues; per-fund object detail for utilities is in basic proprietary statement p6, not duplicated). Water/Sewer/Solid Waste budget-basis actuals (72,191/44,268/94,846) differ from p6 operating expenses for Solid Waste (95,727). Nursing Home (component unit) budget lines not recorded. Library and Community Improvement transfer columns assigned by column position (library net other financing 13,056 checks). Care Center column on p10 has only interest income 970. Read pages 1-10 of 10.",
